<title>UK: Norway's Gullfaks loading 10 crude cargoes in Sept.</title>
<headline>Norway's Gullfaks loading 10 crude cargoes in Sept.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Norway's Gullfaks crude system will load 10 standard 855,000 barrel cargoes in September, a sharp fall from the 19 expected to load in August, traders said.</p>
<p>The total volume will be 8.55 million barrels, down from the original 16.25 million expected in August, the sources added.</p>
<p>The Gullfaks A and B platforms are due to be shut from August 28 to September 15 for summer maintenance, eating dramatically into output volumes.</p>
<p>August's production was already 1.7 million barrels lower than July and 4.26 million barrels below June because of problems with a compressor in the Vigdis oilfield.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 8060</p>
</text>
